      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "The best time to replace a roof in Utah is late spring through early fall (May through October)\n. During this window, mild temperatures and predictable dry weather allow asphalt shingles to properly seal and cure, while helping roofing crews work safely and efficiently.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "late spring through early fall (May through October)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Seasonal Breakdown for Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Late Spring & Summer: Offers stable, warm, and dry conditions ideal for optimal shingle sealing. However, early booking is vital because summer is peak construction season."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Early Fall: Often considered the \"gold standard\". Temperatures are crisp and comfortable for workers, and it prepares your home before heavy mountain and valley snow arrives."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Late Fall & Winter: Challenging due to freezing temperatures, snow, and ice dams. Shingles can become brittle and lose their self-sealing adhesive properties unless special precautions or hand-sealing are used. However, replacements are still done in emergencies (like active leaks)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Factors to Consider"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Beat the Rush: Scheduling in late spring or mid-summer helps you avoid the heavy autumn rush when local contractors are heavily booked."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Weather Vulnerability: Utah's unpredictable spring rainstorms or sudden early freezes can delay or complicate projects if not timed carefully."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Urgency Over Rules: If your roof is actively leaking or severely damaged, the best time to replace it is immediately\u2014waiting for a specific season can lead to costly structural rot or mold."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "The current condition or age\nof your roof"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Your general region in Utah (e.g., Wasatch Front, snowy mountain elevation, or Southern Utah)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can give you more tailored advice or help you look out for specific warning signs."
      }
